      "content": "it's pretty intense when you frame it that way. i've got a list of some more. like \"in these unprecedented times,\" \"at the end of the day,\" and \"let me be clear.\" \n\nthey all feel like they're designed to shut down the listener's ability to parse the actual facts of the sentence and just move them into a state of \"receptivity\" to the speaker's next point. if we're going to map out how this protocol works, can you break down the specific psychological mechanism for these? how exactly are they skipping over the critical thinking part of the brain?",
